  "runId": "af-critique-v3-fileout-ms36mbv2-n5byxo",
  "workflowName": "af_critique_v3_fileout",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: 'af_critique_v3_fileout',\n  description: 'Dual-agent critique v3: agents write full reports to files (bypass return-channel compression), return short confirmations only.'\n};\n\nconst brief = `\nPRODUCT: \"The Armchair Futurist — the last AI consultant you'll ever hire.\" 1:1 AI mastery mentoring. Success = how fast the client stops paying us (self-sufficient in 8-10 weeks). Landing page = 14 sections + embedded 9-question AI-readiness assessment (free, no email to see score).\nAUDIENCE: Established professionals (consultants, coaches, freelancers, agency owners) with existing revenue. Time-poor, skeptical of marketing copy, abandon in <5s. Already pay for AI tools; may have been burned by an \"AI workshop.\"\nBRAND VOICE (direct/warm/expert): Clarity over hype. Trust as the product. Exit as the goal. Capability not deliverable.\nANTI-SLOP KILL LIST: delve, landscape, tapestry, testament, navigate, it's worth noting, first and foremost, in order to, at the end of the day, journey (business metaphor), unlock, leverage, seamless, robust, cutting-edge, game-changer, \"unlock AI's potential\", \"navigate the AI landscape\". Em-dashes capped at ONE per paragraph. Varied sentence rhythm (long/short, fragments, occasional \"And\"/\"But\" opener).\nDESIGN SYSTEM (HP white-paper): Space Grotesk display + Manrope body. ONE signal color HP Electric Blue #024ad8 (every CTA/link/focus ring). Ink #1a1a1a headlines. White canvas, cloud #f7f7f7 cards, 16px radii (cards/photos), 4px (buttons/inputs). Dark navy slabs for testimonials + closing CTA. Buttons = 14px Manrope 600 uppercase +0.7px tracking 4px radius. NO gradients, NO text shadows, NO warm accents, NO rounded-full except avatars/pill tabs.\nANTI-REFERENCES: generic AI-consultant sites (stock photos, buzzword copy, \"+300%\" metric cards, gradient text, glassmorphism); course-platform look (sticky CTAs, \"join 10,000 students\", fake testimonials); SaaS dashboard aesthetic (feature grids, logo walls); AI slop (AI palette, gradient text, Inter everywhere, bounce easing, 3-tier pricing middle-highlighted, blobs).\n`;\n\nconst bundlePath = '/tmp/af_critique_bundle.md';\nconst repo = process.cwd();\nconst outA = repo + '/.impeccable/critique/assessment-A.md';\nconst outB = repo + '/.impeccable/critique/assessment-B.md';\n\nconst assessA = () => agent(\n`You are Assessment A in an Impeccable dual-agent UX/copy critique. Award-winning design director. ISOLATION: do NOT run detect.mjs or any detector — that is Assessment B's job.\n\nRead EXACTLY ONE file: ${bundlePath}. It has, per source file, visible copy, heading tags, aria/alt/role/tabIndex, key classNames for the homepage (src/app/page.tsx), layout, all 16 sections, and the assessment flow. Analyze ONLY from this bundle.\n\nBRIEF:\n${brief}\n\nProduce the full structured report with EXACTLY these 10 sections:\n1. DESIGN-SPECIFICITY VERDICT (paragraph + Grounded/Partially/Generic).\n2. NIELSEN HEURISTICS (0-4 each, n/a only if truly inapplicable; score + specific finding quoting copy + file) for all 10.\n3. COGNITIVE LOAD (a >4-option decision points, b 5-sec first-action failures, c icon-only w/o labels, d jargon) — cite file + quote.\n4. EMOTIONAL JOURNEY (peak-end): walk section order; peaks/valleys; reassurance at high-stakes moments; does \"exit as goal\" survive or get undercut by hard sell?\n5. COPY AUDIT (thorough, from bundle): anti-slop violations (kill-list), em-dash >1/para, voice breaks, unverifiable claims (violates \"density of fact\"), missing \"exit\" framing, clarity/jargon. Then COPY-HEALTH verdict (Strong/Needs Work/Slop Detected) + ranked top copy issues.\n6. STRENGTHS (2-3 specific).\n7. PRIORITY ISSUES (3-5 ranked; file+quote + one-line fix each).\n8. PERSONA RED FLAGS — Jordan, Riley, Casey, + \"Morgan\" (established consultant, already pays for AI, burned by an AI workshop). Per persona.\n9. MINOR OBSERVATIONS (bullets).\n10. PROVOCATIVE QUESTIONS (2-3 for the founder).\n\nDELIVERY: Write the COMPLETE report to the file ${outA} using your file-write tool (create parent dirs). Quote real bundle text with source file names. No hedging. After writing, return ONLY: \"REPORT_A_WRITTEN: <bytes> bytes\" — do not paste the report in your reply.`,\n  { phase: 'Assessment A: Design + Copy Review' }\n);\n\nconst assessB = () => agent(\n`You are Assessment B in an Impeccable dual-agent critique. DETERMINISTIC + a11y/perf EVIDENCE only. ISOLATION: no design opinions; run independently.\n\nRepo: ${repo}. Three steps.\n\nSTEP 1 — DETECTOR (mandatory). Run and capture FULL JSON:\n  node /home/alex/.pi/agent/skills/impeccable/scripts/detect.mjs --json src\nExit 0=clean, 2=findings. Report total count, per-rule counts, rule names, and the file:line list for EVERY finding (keep locations). If missing/error, report exact error + \"deterministic scan unavailable\", continue.\n\nSTEP 2 — BROWSER (do not fabricate). No native browser-canvas tool in subagent sandbox; headless browser not reliably available. SKIP injection; report exactly: \"Browser visualization skipped: no native browser-canvas tool exposed; headless browser not available in subagent sandbox.\" Do not start live-server.\n\nSTEP 3 — STATIC A11y/PERF EVIDENCE. Read ${bundlePath} (per-file copy, headings, aria/alt/role/tabIndex, className samples, flags client/motion/reducedMotion/outlineNone/focusVis/onClickOnly). Report concrete findings (file + what), grouped a-h:\n  a. images without alt / empty alt on meaningful images\n  b. form inputs without visible label / aria-label / required indication (assessment answers + email capture)\n  c. heading order issues (skipped levels, multiple h1)\n  d. click-only interactive (onClickOnly) lacking keyboard handler/role/tabIndex\n  e. focus indicators: outline-none without focus-visible replacement? rings present?\n  f. color-only meaning\n  g. \"use client\" over-use / un-lazy assets / hero CLS-LCP risk / motion-heavy sections\n  h. reduced-motion: which animated sections respect prefers-reduced-motion vs which do not\n\nDELIVERY: Write the COMPLETE evidence report to ${outB} using your file-write tool (create parent dirs). Structure: (1) Detector findings (counts, rule names, file:line list, or unavailable error); (2) Browser (exact skip sentence); (3) Static a11y/perf a-h with file refs; (4) Likely detector false positives vs DESIGN.md; (5) Skipped steps + reasons. After writing, return ONLY: \"REPORT_B_WRITTEN: <bytes> bytes\" — do not paste the report.`,\n  { phase: 'Assessment B: Detector + Browser Evidence' }\n);\n\nconst [a, b] = await parallel([assessA, assessB]);\nlog('confirmations: ' + a + ' | ' + b);\nreturn 'A: ' + a + ' | B: ' + b;",
